  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Center Security Opportunities in the MENA Region Seminar 01-24</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This seminar will look at the MENA region and what it will look like in 3-5 years, including new opportunities for capacity building and regional security cooperation. This five-day seminar will focus on developing opportunities for regional security coordination in the MENA region including Border Security, the use of Unmanned Aerial Vehicles, efforts to counter violent extremism, De-Mining Efforts, Cyber Security, Maritime Security, Climate Change, refugees and vulnerable populations, and Energy and Water Security. It will include participants from the defense, security and diplomatic establishment. This seminar will provide a venue for participants to explore and self-identify areas of cooperation, areas of disagreement, and develop proposals to promote progress. By hearing different viewpoints and voices and establishing personal relationships, participants will be more likely to constructively explore ways to advance cooperation and strengthen trust as a strategic national interest for all parties.</narrative>
  </description>
